Welcome to this part of A practical RAG classroom handbook. Our focus is ingestion and evidence. Token chunking divides text into manageable pieces. In this teaching example the chunk size is 512 tokens and the overlap is 50 tokens. Overlap repeats a small boundary region so a sentence near an edge has additional context. A token is not always a complete word.

