Welcome to this part of A practical RAG classroom handbook. Our focus is three storage destinations. Vector storage holds embeddings that support similarity search by meaning. A BM25 corpus supports lexical matching, which is useful for exact references such as ATLAS-LAB-73. A graph stores extracted entities and relationships such as a coordinator leading a group. These representations serve different purposes.

