Welcome to this part of A practical RAG classroom handbook. Our focus is evaluation and missing answers. Faithfulness asks whether the answer is supported by retrieved evidence. Relevance asks whether it addresses the question. Context precision concerns the usefulness of retrieved material. These concepts should be demonstrated with examples rather than interpreted as guarantees of correctness.

